CHAPTER ONE: FIGHT TO WIN
Other Paths
The Garou fighting for Gaia are
scattered across the world, each pack and
sept with their own ideas for how to fight
the Wyrm. Many would like to believe there’s a
clear distinction between themselves and the Garou
considered to have strayed from the path, but that’s
not true. It’s not uncommon for two septs to consider
each other dangerously wrongheaded or even
downright heretical. Just such a schism is responsible
for the departure of the Cult of Fenris and the
Stargazers and the shattering of the Garou Nation.
Still, the truth is that sometimes it’s a Moon Cult
inventing a powerful new method for attacking
the enemy. Their idiosyncratic interpretations of
spirit hierarchies may have surprisingly concrete
results in the creation of Rites or Talismans that
the werewolves fighting for Gaia would have never
thought of. How to deal with that is a test of
character for any Garou. Can you accept the tools
of those who have betrayed Gaia if they work? Some
argue that to win, all methods are acceptable, while
others fear being tainted by the methods of the likes
of the Cult of Fenris.
Famous Garou
The characters voicing their opinions in this
chapter are all famous Garou, known for
their various exploits. Their stories are told at
moots and many have met them, building their
legends still further. Their Loresheets can be
found in the book Shattered Nation.
