Apocalypse, and now Gaia is dying. And we with it. Or she with us.
Dagrack was the leader of the Black Spiral Dancers who also wanted the Silver
Crown of the Garou Nation. She managed to grab the crown and place it on her
head. She was not worthy and the crown burned her whole head. I wish I’d thought
of that. Using your enemy’s plans against them.
I was once skinned alive with a silver knife and my teeth were pulled out. Fuck,
that hurt like hell. But Lord Arkady made a fatal mistake: he didn’t kill me. We
Garou can heal. And when we Rage, we heal fast. You should always kill an enemy
Garou and make sure they’re really dead. I should’ve killed Lord Arkady and not
just banish him.
When in doubt, you should always consult the Litany. The Tenets are full of wisdom.
You can’t smell the Wyrm. Sometimes you can’t even see it. But you can see its
effects. Whether that oil worker was a fomori or not doesn’t matter. They were
killing Gaia. They deserved to die. I met his family later and explained why I had to
kill him. They didn’t thank me. But I did it for them, too.
There are Black Spiral Dancers everywhere. Maybe you’re one of them.
Pentex has a lot of fronts. If there were enough of us, we could take them all
down. It’s not a mythological beast that just grows more heads. If we had managed
to down enough of them, even Pentex would’ve died. If only.
The Apocalypse came and went, taking the glory of the Garou with it.
I once witnessed a Wyld-spirit possess an elephant at a circus. The beast went
wild and trampled its wrangler and many people in the audience. There was chaos
and death. I could’ve killed the elephant but I didn’t. It felt like it was my kin
somehow. Maybe it was Gaia’s will that those people die?
I sometimes think all humans are possessed by Weaver gafflings.
