Tender of Banes
Many Garou follow the Litany to a fault and will always
combat the Wyrm wherever it dwells and whenever it thrives.
The question arises: what is combat? When you destroy the same
Bane over and over again, each time thinking it will turn out differently
than the last, it feels less like combat and more like insanity.
The role of Bane Tender is very common among the members of the
Ghost Council, with some stories saying that they were the first tribe to
perform the Rite of Binding as a solution to Banes. Binding a Bane that
cannot be destroyed by normal means would seem like a good solution,
but like anything touched by the Wyrm, it is not that simple. These seals
need to be kept in order and need to be attended. A Bane Tender must be
sure that no one attempts to release the Bane, or that the influence of a
Bane on the surrounding area is not significant.
After the shattering of the Garou Nation, the rise of the Cult of
Fenris, and the subsequent passing of many older werewolves, many
complications revolve around the Bane Tenders. With them gone,
substantial volumes of old seals remain unattended, turning them into
impending disaster zones when the Bane escapes.
