Urge Wyrms
Although the Triatic Wyrms are
powerful, they’re also abstract in their own
way. Many Garou are more familiar with
the Urge Wyrms, said to represent the various urges
comprising the psyche of the Wyrm. Or perhaps
that’s mere projection, and they’re instead the allpowerful
impulses in the hearts of humanity feeding
the Wyrm in the first place.
In terms of power and presence, the Urge Wyrms
are comparable to the great Patron Spirits of the
tribes of Gaia. They’re too powerful to be interacted
with personally, but their symbolic and metaphysical
power is felt through the Umbra.
The Urge Wyrms are particularly important
for the Black Spiral Dancers, who may have been
responsible for the names they now have among
the Garou. In the stories of the Black Spiral
Dancers, the Urge Wyrms make the Wyrm more
comprehensible, attributing human motivations
and emotions to it. Whether this reflects what the
Wyrm is really like or is just an artifact of Spiral
mythology is anybody’s guess.
Abhorra, Urge of Hatred
If it’s true that the Urge Wyrms represent different
facets and impulses in the personality of the Wyrm,
the origins of Abhorra, the Urge of Hatred, are not
hard to fathom. Being imprisoned by the Weaver
caused an enduring hatred of the pattern to erupt,
making order the prime target for the Wyrm’s
seething enmity.
The Urge of Hatred is attracted to wherever
people start to see themselves surrounded by hostile
forces, attributing their failures and misfortune
to individuals and groups they come to see as
subhuman and vile. Self-loathing is at the root of
the Urge, turned outwards in displays of seething
malevolence.
Strangling Hands
Hatred is not just an emotion. Hatred is the hand
that strikes, chokes, and reaches out to hurt. There
have been enough such hands caressing human
bodies before their touch turns violent that they
have their manifestations in the Umbra too, lurking
in the shadows, ready to crawl along the warm skin
of someone whose mere existence offends them.
When possessing a human, a Strangling Hand
is not content to seethe. Hatred is action, and that
action manifests when a person gets their hands on
the loved ones they hate. Those possessed are rarely
strong, for the Strangling Hands specialize in the
weak victimizing the weaker.
What Does It Want? The Strangling Hand wants
to strangle. It wants control in the rudimentary form
of being able to touch and grasp and kill.
Possession / Manifestation: In the Umbra, the
Strangling Hand is not particularly conspicuous
due to its small size. It looks like a wiry, weathered
human hand with unusually long fingernails and
knotty joints, crawling and climbing. It prefers to
stay in cover, hiding from anyone capable of striking
back. When it possesses humans, their hands can’t
stay still, often reaching out to grasp.
