WYRMTIDE
Oubliette
The fear of loneliness claims everyone in the city.
And it is that feeling that the Oubliette feeds on.
It feeds off the isolation in the worst capitalistic
hellholes of modern society, creating mindscapes
and visions that continue to isolate people from one
another. This, in turn, has created the Oubliette.
As people are more and more isolated through the
influence of the Oubliette, it finally strikes as it reels
them into its trap, a pocket of liminal space on the
edge of the Spirit Wilds — an alley that they never
escape from, labyrinthine hallways in their own
apartment building. The Oubliette creates these
tormented hellscapes of solitude, driving people to
give up and embrace nothingness to feed the Bane.
What Does It Want? Garou are defined by their
packs, tribes, and septs. As such, they’re anathema
to the Oubliette who finds their social ties actively
offensive. They must be broken apart!
Possession/Manifestation: The Oubliette often
refrains from possessing anything sentient but
instead manifests inside decrepit buildings and old
machinery. Inside of the Umbra, the Oubliette is a
slim, many-limbed and faceless creature, with a maw
opening in its chest, revealing a pit of nothingness.
Oubliette Spirit
Power: 6–10
Exceptional Dice Pools: Insight +3, Persuasion
+3, Intimidation +4
Notes/Other Traits:
Manifesting Dread: Once per scene, the
Oubliette can possess objects near their intended
target for the purpose of making them act in a
menacing manner.
