Karnala, Urge of Desire
There is something seductive about the Urge of
Desire. Is it so bad to want things? The tribes of
Gaia desire to free the world from the devastation of
human greed. We all desire what’s best for those we
love. Surely that’s not an Urge Wyrm?
Said to have been born out of the Wyrm’s desire
for freedom, Karnala represents yearning based
on a desire for gratification at the expense of
everything else. Nothing and nobody matters as
long as you get what you need. Karnala feeds when
desire turns malignant, even the most altruistic
or justified motivations twisting into something
selfish, shortsighted, and destructive. After all, even
the desires born of love can become the need to
control and limit.
Embracers
Many human Wyrm cults believe when spirits
of love, lust, kinship, or yearning turn to the
Wyrm, they become Embracers. Some cultists
summon them to humiliate their enemies or to gain
someone’s affections.
Anyone feeling the pangs of an emotional or
physical desire is susceptible to its influence. The
Bane encourages their targets into developing deeper
and more twisted obsessions and to claim the focus
of these obsessions by any means necessary.
What Does It Want? Embracers crave
gratification of all kinds and see others (including
the people they influence) as a means to that end.
