WYRMTIDE
Khaaloobh, Urge of Indulgence
Why not just give in? Accept the loss, the entropy,
the chaos. Whether the mess you’ve made of your
own life or the depredations of others, wouldn’t it
be easiest just to indulge? Making a thing of it won’t
help, and it’s nicer to just lie down and luxuriate in
your own filth.
The Urge of Indulgence is multifaceted.
Sometimes it’s seen to represent consumption or
decay, the eroding of morals and principles as much
as physical loss of form. It’s strengthened when
ideals, principles, and best practices devolve into a
morass of shortcuts and selfish shortsightenedness.
Raucous Whirlwinds
The Black Spiral Dancers claim the Raucous
Whirlwinds as their brethren. They say back in
the War of Rage, the Garou hunted wereboars
to extinction, and their spirits fled into the Black
Labyrinth. Now they eternally celebrate their pact,
leaving bodies and Banelands in their wake.
Raucous Whirlwinds seek out the sybaritic or the
nihilistic in the physical world and use their bodies
to get the party started.
What Does It Want? The Raucous Whirlwind’s
celebration feast won’t end until the entire Umbra’s
devoured, and they bring their celebration to the
physical world knowing full well their victims’
indulgence leads to their death. It’s a festival for the
Apocalypse, after all.
Possession / Manifestation: Within the Umbra,
Raucous Whirlwinds appear as boars with fleshless
heads. Strong, hazy winds surround them, hiding
their true appearance. Possessed hosts’ bodies grow
gaunt and their eyes develop the pupils of a boar.
