Pseulak, Urge of Lies
The very first lie told by the Wyrm was to itself,
trying to pretend it hadn’t failed to contain the
Weaver. Out of this self-deception Pseulak was
born. It is the Urge Wyrm of lies, regardless of
whether you’re lying to others or yourself. Its
influence can initially be minor: We all need white
lies to survive. Who really wants to dwell on all
of our failures? Better come up with stories that
let us off the hook. The subtle nature of Pseulak’s
power is in how those stories build and grow
until they’ve become all-encompassing untruths
trapping us within.
The Urge of Lies gains power from small human
fibs and extravagant corporate and government
propaganda. Every time a politician lies to start a
war or a prophet uses God to justify their personal
excesses, Pseulak smiles in contentment.
