Hunger Vortex
All types of Banes thrived during the Californian
genocide of the Indigenous population. Starvation
was one of the biggest killers, reaching far and
wide. So many starved to death that the numerous
Scavenger Packs turned on other Banes to sate their
hunger. The frenzied horde of Banes kept eating
until they consumed even themselves. Out of that
ouroboros, the Hunger Vortex was created as it
gestated beneath the earth — born out of all the
greed, poison, kidnappings, and hatred that had
amalgamated during the famine.
It awoke several times afterwards, and just as many
times, the Hunger Vortex was defeated by scores
of theurges working together despite their tribe
and differences, sacrificing themselves to save their
peoples from starvation.
As the wildfires of today rage and crops wither
without water, the Hunger Vortex stirs once more
beneath the dust of the Californian desert. The
question is whether there are any packs that have
the knowledge and the courage to fight it and send it
back to sleep.
If the Bane is still asleep, it is possible to perform
the Rite of Binding to keep it locked away for
another summer. If it wakes up, the Hunger
Vortex’s defeat will require answers found in the
deepest Umbra, a type of journey that will often
involve self-sacrifice.
What Does It Want? Everybody and everything
consumes things around them. This is a simple fact
represented by the Hunger Vortex. What makes it
interesting is that hunger can consume so much
more: culture, ideas, a whole people.
Possession/Manifestation: When the Hunger
Vortex takes someone’s body, they become dried
out, and their body slowly consumes itself. That
possession can last for years, and the hosts just grow
more emaciated. When manifesting as itself, it is a
colossal vortex of dark dust with faces and shapes
of countless stolen lives that can be seen contorting
within. Around it you can sense inescapable hunger
and desperation.
