the Howl is the Strontium Machine, a useless engine
expressly designed to do nothing but waste fuel and
blast out vile fumes. For an individual pack, the
Strontium Engine is usually built into a car for ease
of transportation, while a large hive might feature a
huge furnace blasting fire in all directions, fed by the
Howl night and day.
According to their own legends, the Strontium
Howl are the descendants of the ravening armies
marching ever onward, eating entire villages clean of
everything they had like a cloud of locusts. They talk
of a grand history of military victories and heroic
sacrifice in the service of martial values of death and
destruction.
These stories are lies designed to give the lost and
disaffected members of the tribe an identity as a
heroic vanguard. In reality, the cult is a phenomenon
of the Apocalypse, less than ten years old yet
massively successful as it spreads across desert
highways across the world.
The Howl loves cars, gasoline, military hardware,
and big explosions. Flair is at least as important as
functionality since the members of the cult build
vehicles for their initiation Rites and celebrations.
Prospective members must face off against a tank
or a similar improbably large vehicle in combat
and survive. Before they pass the initiation,
prospects can be abused by any Howl who feels
like it. Such abuse occurs post-initiation too, but
now the new member is allowed to hit back. After
passing the initiation, new members are subjected
to a scarification Rite, the effects of which are
permanent. During the Rite, members of the new
Howl’s pack are invited to vandalize their body in
whatever fashion they find amusing.
The Strontium Howl is organized much like a
gang, with individual chapters coming together for
larger events where the broader agenda of the cult
is determined. The cult has leaders but they change
often, rarely lasting longer than a year.
Strontium is a holy substance for the Howl
because of the way it interacts with the body. It’s
radioactive and poisonous, yet the bodies of humans
and animals mistake it for calcium and use it to build
bone and teeth. A nuclear meltdown leads to entire
populations having the poison of the Wyrm form
the very infrastructure of their bodies.
Some Strontium Howl seek to ingest strontium
on purpose to make this happen, although the
prodigious healing powers of the Garou and the short
lifespan of the average Black Spiral Dancer mean that
they don’t see as many ill effects as you’d think.
In the worldview of the Howl, the Apocalypse
is now and the Spirals must live according to the
strictures of the Wyrm, embodying destruction in
their very beings. They tend to see other Black Spiral
cults as weak losers who don’t have what it takes to
really live a life of devastation.
Patron Spirits
In addition to Bat, venerated by all Black Spiral
Dancers, individual packs of Strontium Howl
often have Patron Spirits of radioactivity, internal
combustion engines, smog, and other modern
manifestations of industrial devastation. The
cult particularly values everything connected to
radioactivity, and such things become all the more
sacred because they’re so difficult to obtain.
Acquiring actual radioactive materials is seen as a
surefire way to gain the favor of the spirits.
Personalities
The Strontium Howl are former soldiers, members
of motorcycle gangs, drifters, and violent criminals.
They like guns, cars, fire, and violence.
Swollen Tongue
A lean, scarred, and tattooed man always leaning
on something, Swollen Tongue got his name when
his packmates ripped off his lower jaw during his
initiation to the Howl. His tongue lolls out of the hole
in his face, longer than it has any right to be. He is
111
CHAPTER THREE: THE POISON SEEPS IN
unable to bite but his claws more than make up for it.
An ahroun, Swollen Tongue has a reputation for
always being the first to attack the enemy, often
driving a motorcycle to crash into them as he jumps
off and shifts into crinos, his tongue trailing saliva.
Something of an innovator among the Howl,
Swollen Tongue has a knack for coming up with new
games that are even more dangerous and stupid than
before. His current favorite is Crash Test Dummies,
where Garou simply crash into each other in various
vehicles. Allegedly, Swollen Tongue himself survived
having his car overrun by a tank.
