Zhyzhak
Often described as the most powerful Garou alive,
Zhyzhak is a legendary figure among both the
shattered Nation and the Black Spiral Dancers.
Stories of her origins tend towards the mythical,
whether they tell of how she was born of a giant
Wyrmsnake deep in the Umbra or clawed her way
out of her mother’s womb. Whatever the truth, she’s
an ahroun of immense power and ability, towering
over her lesser brethren and able to vanquish entire
packs of Garou by herself.
Tall, muscular, and black-haired, Zhyzhak likes to
dress for effect, favoring spikes, black leather, and combat
boots. She wields a scourge, a Talisman allowing her to
rip the meat off the bones of her enemies.
Although Zhyzhak often recruits members to her
pack from the Strontium Howl, it’s not clear if she
actually considers herself a member of the cult. Her
status among the Black Spiral Dancers transcends
whatever affiliation she may hold, and she’s even
venerated by Dancers who typically detest the
Strontium Howl.
Those who have met her say that Zhyzhak hears the
voice of the Wyrm inside her mind. Her actions are
