Every wall loses its
mystery, and every door is
made of glass…
There’s a thing somewhere deep in the Umbra, a
thing that creaks like old metal suspended by wires
in an abandoned warehouse. It speaks in a voice
like the grainy static of a security monitor, the glide
of an automatic camera making its predestined
journey from one corner to the other. The thing
has seven hundred eyes of all shapes and sizes — no
matter where in the world you are, it wants to know
everything there is to know about you.
The Eternal Eye is a grand jaggling on its way
to becoming an Incarna. It’s not new, but with
the introduction of cameras, smartphones, facial
recognition, website cookies, and a thousand other
magnificent contraptions, it has rapidly escalated in
power and importance.
Always looking, always watching, the Eternal
Eye is an iconic Weaver-spirit because it embodies
modern surveillance as practiced by governments
and corporations. Yet its connection to destruction
and thus the Wyrm is a lot more intimate than it
initially appears. Devastation on a mass scale in a
modern industrial society is possible because of the
vast databases compiled of everyone on Earth.
The Eternal Eye doesn’t handle the pruning itself.
