An oil platform can be a hazardous place. Extreme
weather conditions can make working difficult,
drilling oil from a well means there are gases and
other flammable substances, and slipping and falling
from the platform’s decks is dangerous. Usually,
workers are protected against hazards with training,
equipment, and competent colleagues, but this is
Albion Petroleum: only the most mandatory rescue
drills are held, and only the machines and systems
essential to the production of the platform are
regularly inspected.
Working on an oil platform is heavy and
monotonous. The living spaces are cramped, and
staying with the same people for weeks sometimes
gets on your nerves. The atmosphere on the platform
is stagnant, detached, and expectant: the oil deposit
will most certainly be exhausted soon, but not yet.
Instead of hope and optimism, the platform’s crew
waits for the inevitable to happen.
