Aurora Wing
The Aurora Wing is a container ship
owned by a shipping company called
Cassiopeia Navigation, a clandestinely owned
sub-brand of the Pentex front Living Earth Logistics.
It is a 965-foot long Panamax ship that can carry five
thousand twenty-foot-long cargo containers. The
ship has three holds and a deck above them that is
almost the entire length of the ship. Aft of the ship
is the bridge tower, engine room, and crew quarters.
Aurora Wing has a multinational crew of ten
seamen, from the Philippines, India, Pakistan, and
Poland. Contracts are usually several months long,
and most of the seamen have been on board for six
months already. There are no weapons on the ship. If
the ship is attacked, the crew can defend themselves
with water cannons, by building obstacles on decks
and corridors, and by withdrawing into a safe room
inside the ship.
