Why the Players’ Pack?
The characters’ sept is in danger. If they don’t act,
not only will they lose something they worked so
hard to build, but they could also lose friends and
allies to the Black Spiral Dancers (through murder
or desertion).
Goals
The players have three goals. The first is to thwart
the Black Spiral Dancers. The second is to unmask
the traitor in the sept. The third is to complete the
Rite of Caern Building (see Werewolf, p. 185.)
As the Storyteller, you have two goals. The first
is to make that location as interesting and useful
as possible, even before it becomes a caern. The
second is to establish enemies for future stories,
whether they’re the Dancers in this story or an
escaped traitor.
Supporting Characters
This story uses the following characters:
Heart’s Whisper: As an ahroun Bone Gnawer old
enough to have witnessed the Garou Nation’s fall,
Heart’s Whisper has seen many horrors. She views
her role as the Rite master for this would-be caern as
a step towards a brighter future. Consider replacing
her role in this story with either a Mentor the pack
already has, or a pack member who took the Rite of
Caern Building.
Mercy: Short for “Mercy Kill,” this Black Spiral
Dancer leads a well-prepared force. He received word
of the Rite happening on his pack’s territory from
Embraces-The-Sky and called reinforcements. Once
he wipes everyone out, he’ll help his pack claim the
caern for the Dancers.
Embraces-The-Sky: The galliard Silver Fang is
burnt out. Only a bad day away from harano, he
