not long after the sept began the Rite and found
Dancer philosophy more palatable than he realized.
Though he intends to sell out the sept and dance the
Black Spiral, he still hopes the situation ends with
little bloodshed.
Locations
This story takes place in the soon-to-be caern. Here
are a few options where that caern could be located.
Dusty’s Cave: This large cave in a national forest is
open to the public, and a sept member’s connections
give them usage of the land. Its widespread tunnel
system can be used to create bottlenecks.
Plenty Stop #4561: Corporate shut down this
store months ago, and it stands as an empty husk.
A sept member bought it in hopes of reviving the
store’s spirits. The standing aisles and copious
backrooms make for great cover and hiding places.
Harvest Inn: This three-story inn is situated in
the very heart of a bustling city. Someone the sept
once helped granted them access to the building.
The building is well stocked for an extended siege,
and its penthouse on the third story is a great
lookout point.
Scenes
The following is a possible structure of this story.
The Hook: Caern Raising
The sept decides to expand their holdings and
create another caern. Unlike the other hooks, this
story’s hook could be a story of its own. Creating a
new caern involves repairing the actual structure,
negotiation with the local spirits, and ensuring the
process conforms to the phases of the moon.
As the pack helps with these preparations, they
should start seeing warning signs. Embraces-The-
Sky makes long absences. Other sept members catch
glimpses of figures watching them in the distance.
Newly allied spirits caution them about “the
neighbors” but don’t have the full details.
Rising Action: First Wave
With the lunar cycle ending, the sept gathers. Heart’s
Whisper leads the Rite with skill and aplomb.
A Wits + Awareness or Investigation test at
Difficulty 3 alerts the pack that something’s wrong
before the Black Spiral Dancers strike. Unless any
sept member has a reason to dismiss or distrust the
pack, the rest of the sept will notice and join the pack
if they strike first. Even Embraces-The-Sky joins the
fight in hopes that it’ll end soon or the Dancers can
take him away in the chaos.
This first wave is on the lower rungs of their social
hierarchy. They amount to slightly more than half
of the present sept members. What they lack in
equipment, prowess with Gifts, or combat ability,
they make up for with zeal and a need to prove
themselves in the eyes of their superiors. They waste
no time attacking and attempt to apprehend as many
sept members as possible.
The Dancers know many of the sept’s members
by name and even have a basic idea of what they’re
capable of. The pack members are always included in
that number.
The Midpoint: Traitor Hunting
After the first wave of Dancers is defeated, most
of the sept successfully hunkers down, or three
full rounds of Conflict, whichever comes first, any
surviving Dancers make a tactical retreat. The pack
has a short moment of respite to recover wounds and
check on who’s still standing.
Embraces-The-Sky tells anyone in earshot that
he’s going to “check if they’re still out there.” An
Intelligence + Insight test at Difficulty 3 or the
successful use of Gaia’s Candor reveals his lie.
If revealed as traitor, Embraces-The-Sky makes
a run for it, and the pack can ask for the help of
any allies in earshot to help give chase. If the sept
hunkered down somewhere the Dancers couldn’t
find, he tries to reveal their location. He’ll fight to
the death to escape.
If Heart’s Whisper joined the pack in chasing
Embraces-The-Sky down, he attacks her at the first
