Stories
The Arcanum is great for showing how the Garou
look from an outside perspective. They don’t have
anything in particular against werewolves, but
they’re curious. Sometimes, their studies involve
taking important Talismans and other Garou
cultural artifacts and locking them away.
Deed of Ownership: A local caern, perhaps
even a dead one, is being acquired by a new owner:
Deborah King. By the time the pack learns of
someone acquiring the land surrounding the caern,
the deal is almost done. Debborah’s agents might
not threaten the pack or sept, but their studies
anger the local spirits. Their urge for fame, power,
or knowledge may attract multiple Banes.
Questions Are Being Asked: Numerous
connections on the Relationship Map explain that
a stranger has been asking about one or more of the
players’ characters. Aiden Jones, a young and cocky
new member of the chapterhouse, has been acting
on his own to research local spirits and hopes to track
down the pack member to answer his questions. Aiden
catches up with the pack at the most inopportune or
dangerous moments, firmly believing the pack won’t
let any harm come to him. If harm comes to him, the
chapter members use their knowledge and influence to
make life difficult for the pack.
Secret Knowledge: The pack is in need of some
occult item or knowledge, whether the name of a spirit
to be bargained with, information on how to reawaken
a caern, materials needed for a rare Rite, or a Talisman
thought lost ages ago. Each attempt to procure it is
foiled, as the same Arcanum agent was there days or
hours before the pack. Why would someone else need
the same thing as the pack? What lengths will the pack
go to in order to retrieve what they need?
Fall
A chapterhouse is relatively well defended, for
a group of humans. Many have silver weapons
available, and they often take advantage of any
Garou’s Folkloric Banes, Blocks, or Tells. A few can
even counter a Garou’s Gifts or are protected by
spirits bound by the Arcanum members. That said,
