Hihiro Tomkins
After two combat tours, Special Agent Tomkins
was ready to do anything for his country. Or so he
thought. Delirium and the mind-twisting powers
of other things that go bump in the night broke
that belief, leaving him wounded in ways no IED or
enemy fireteam could match.
A shattered man, he’s now a ticking time bomb
of government secrets, expert military training, and
disavowed intel cobbled together by what’s left of
his scarred mind. A walking failure of the system to
care for its veterans, he lives in squalor, spreading
half-remembered rhetoric that no one believes until
he can pull together the disparate scraps of truth that
could prove invaluable for local Garou.
